What value is printed to the console?

Examine the code below:

```java
int[][] scores = {
    {5, 7, 9},
    {6, 8, 10}
};
int total = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < scores.length; r++) {
    total += scores[r][1];
}
System.out.println(total);
```
What value is printed after the loop finishes?

Consider the following Java code. What is the exact 2‑dimensional array returned by the call `mystery(matrix)`?

```java
public class Mystery {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] matrix = {
            {1, 2, 3},
            {4, 5, 6},
            {7, 8, 9}
        };
        int[][] result = mystery(matrix);
        // result is printed for inspection
    }

    public static int[][] mystery(int[][] m) {
        int rows = m.length;        
        int cols = m[0].length;      
        int[][] t = new int[cols][rows];
        for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < cols; j++) {
                t[j][i] = m[i][j];   
            }
        }
        return t;
    }
}
```

What will be the contents of the 2‑D array `M` after the following code executes?

```java
int[][] M = {
    {5, 2, 8},
    {1, 4, 7},
    {9, 0, 3},
    {6, 6, 6}
};

int temp;
for (int c = 0; c < M[0].length; c++) {
    temp = M[1][c];
    M[1][c] = M[3][c];
    M[3][c] = temp;
}
```

Select the correct representation of `M` (rows shown in order, each row in brackets).
